            <title>[LU-21083] sanity test_119s: ERANGE restoring max_pages_per_rpc=1024 on ARM</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21083</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_119s returns 34 on review-ldiskfs-arm (EL8.10 x86_64 servers, Rocky9.8 aarch64 client). After raising OST brw_size and remounting, the test sets osc.*.max_pages_per_rpc=16M, then its EXIT trap attempts to restore the saved value 1024 and fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;error: set_param: setting osc/.../max_pages_per_rpc=1024: Numerical result out of range&lt;br/&gt;
test_119s returned 34&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current failure: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/5b9399ef-9760-4db8-a3aa-d095c7ae1827" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/5b9399ef-9760-4db8-a3aa-d095c7ae1827&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/baf30687-7768-407f-9a96-76206e1084d1" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/baf30687-7768-407f-9a96-76206e1084d1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Change 69318 PS2, revision 53236866c207, only changes SSH command handling in test-framework.sh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same detailed sequence and ERANGE restoring 1024 occurred before this patch on change 68413 PS1 on 2026-08-27:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/0d62653d-f2d9-43dc-b0b0-f5f967da9e32" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/0d62653d-f2d9-43dc-b0b0-f5f967da9e32&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
and change 67696 PS6 on 2026-08-30:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/8726d596-f570-41b4-a4db-a782e22f8b64" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/8726d596-f570-41b4-a4db-a782e22f8b64&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Both are review-ldiskfs-arm. Logs were compared, not just the generic returned-34 message.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow shows 3 failures / 1075 non-skipped review-ldiskfs-arm runs over 120 days (1072 passes); 1 / 300 over the last 30 days. These rates cover this subtest's errors, not a controlled reproduction. No local guest reproduction was needed to establish that this predates the patch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test was added by 54431bbfc0 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20520" title="Large unaligned bulk write hangs when client and server page sizes differ" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20520"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20520&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;), already in the base. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20520" title="Large unaligned bulk write hangs when client and server page sizes differ" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20520"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20520&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; covers a bulk-write hang, not this parameter restoration failure. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18739" title="max_pages_per_rpc gives &amp;quot;out of range&amp;quot; error for values less than 1M" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18739"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18739&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; describes sizes below 1M, and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-6421" title="Failed to set max_pages_per_rpc permanently" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-6421"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-6421&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; describes persistent settings lost across remounts; neither covers this failure. Searches for the test name, max_pages_per_rpc with range, and max_pages_per_rpc with 1024 found no matching ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On a 64KiB-page client, 1024 pages is 64MiB, above the 16MiB RPC bound. max_rpc_store treats bare numbers above PTLRPC_MAX_BRW_PAGES as byte values, which also makes 1024 invalid. The test saves the parameter after remount; investigate why it can read this value and ensure valid restoration. The precise source of the saved value has not been reproduced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69318-ps2-e012cf35989e on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69318" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69318&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
